@base <http://ecareathome-ontology.mpi.aass.oru.se/patterns/SmartHome_Geometry.owl> .

<http://ecareathome-ontology.mpi.aass.oru.se/patterns/SmartHome_Geometry.owl> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                                                               owl:imports <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl> ;
                                                                               terms:description "Ontology design pattern for modeling smarthome geometry relationships and concepts."^^xsd:string ;
                                                                               terms:title "Smarthome Geometry Pattern"^^xsd:string ;
                                                                               cpannotationschema:coversRequirements "What are the spatial entities (objects with geometry) in a smart home environment?"^^xsd:string ;
                                                                               cpannotationschema:isSpecializationOf "This pattern is a spacializayion of the GeoSPARQL ontology (http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql) in order to be used in the definition of spatial entities (e.g. places or physical objects) in a smart environment."^^xsd:string ;
                                                                               rdfs:comment """Curated by OntoBoard 1.155.0, so that the pattern passes ODK's quality report with its default profile, names every term with a label, and is consistent and coherent. Changes: label added x26; term declared x4;
- header: dcterms:title \"Smarthome Geometry Pattern\" - the library's name for the pattern
- header: dcterms:description - the library's description of the pattern
Each change is listed under \"curated\" in the pattern's metadata.json in OntoBoard's pattern library."""@en .

